# Web SEO: Agent-host ecosystems

Vendor-aligned **first-class channel** relationships (Meta Muse ↔ Facebook/Instagram/Threads, Grok Bot ↔ X, OpenClaw/Dots ↔ OpenAI-personal-agents sibling grids). Single module: **`web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/ecosystems/index.ts`**.

Host picker scenarios stay in **`agents/decision-scenarios.ts`**. UI archetypes stay in **`agents/host-profiles.ts`** — do not conflate with ecosystem ids.

## Profiles (`AgentHostEcosystemId`)

| Id | Host slugs (`AGENT_HOST_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`) | First-class channels | Typical MCP pin (`relatedMcpSlugs`) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `meta-consumer` | `meta-muse` | `facebook`, `instagram`, `threads` | `muse-code` |
| `openai-personal-agents` | `openclaw`, `dots` | — (sibling agents on host landings) | `chatgpt` |
| `xai-grok` | `grok-bot` | `x` | `cursor` |

Extend **`ECOSYSTEM_PROFILES`**, **`AGENT_HOST_ECOSYSTEM_BY_SLUG`**, and **`audienceTailoredCardByHostSlug`** together when adding a mapped host.

## Where copy runs

| Surface | Entry | Ecosystem behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`/agents/{host}`** | `getPublicAgentHostBySlug` → `withAgentHostEcosystem` (`agents/index.ts`) | Fourth WhoIsFor card; `buildAgentHostEcosystemFaqItems`; hub channel grid sort + badges via `sortAgentChannelHubLinks` |
| **`/agents/{host}/{channel}`** | `buildAgentChannelLandingVm` | `resolveAgentChannelAudienceCards`, `buildAgentChannelEcosystemHeroDescription`, `buildAgentChannelEcosystemFaqItems` |
| **`/channels/{slug}`** | `getPublicChannelBySlug` → `withChannelPageSeoCopy` (`channels/index.ts`) | **Inverse** emphasis: ecosystem fourth card (`buildPublicChannelEcosystemAudienceTailoredCard`), first-card hook (`applyPublicChannelPageAudienceFirstCardHook`), prepended FAQs (`buildPublicChannelEcosystemFaqItems`, dedupe by title), then `PUBLIC_CHANNELS_HUB_FAQ_ITEM_IDS` |
| **`/channels/{slug}` grids** | `channelPageSeo.ts`, grid copy utils, `listPublicAgentIntegrationsForChannel` | Pinned agent hosts (`CHANNEL_PAGE_PINNED_AGENT_SLUGS`); MCP sort via `sortAgentIntegrationsForEcosystem` + primary host from `getPrimaryAgentHostSlugForChannelPage`; sibling badges (`enrichPublicChannelSiblingGridItems`) |

Channel seeds keep **three** base `audienceCards` + optional seed-only **`audienceTailoredCard`** (e.g. LinkedIn). Do **not** duplicate ecosystem fourth cards in `catalog/platforms/{slug}.ts` — runtime getters merge them.

Generic fallback when no ecosystem: **`buildPublicChannelAgentAudienceTailoredCard`** in `channelPageSeo.ts`.

## Key symbols (channel page)

- `getChannelPageEcosystemId`, `getPrimaryAgentHostSlugForChannelPage`
- `buildPublicChannelEcosystemAudienceTailoredCard`, `buildPublicChannelEcosystemFaqItems`
- `buildPublicChannelAgentIntegrationsGridTitle(platformLabel, channelSlug)` — pass **`channelSlug`** from templates for ecosystem titles
- `buildPublicChannelSiblingGridDescription(platformLabel, channelSlug)`

## FAQ deduplication

- Host seed FAQs + `buildAgentHostEcosystemFaqItems` must not repeat the same **`title`** (tests in `ecosystems.test.ts`).
- Channel pages: prepend ecosystem FAQs only when titles are absent from seed **`faqItems`**.
- OpenAI-personal-agents host ecosystem FAQ builder intentionally returns `[]` — use host **`buildAgentHostPickerFaqDescription`** on OpenClaw/Dots seeds instead.

## Tests

| File | Covers |
| --- | --- |
